text:
John buys 2 pairs of shoes for each of his 3 children.  The cost of each pair of shoes is $60.  Therefore, the total cost of the shoes is:

$$
2 \text{ pairs} \times 3 \text{ children} \times 60 \text{ dollars/pair} = 360 \text{ dollars}
$$

John paid a total of $360 for the shoes.

Final answer: \boxed{360}
